    "id": "p5-q39-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "39",
    "prompt": "Expand and simplify $\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt3}\\right)^4$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{49}{36}+\\frac59\\sqrt6$\n\nUse Pascal coefficients $1,4,6,4,1$, then simplify the surds.",
      "worked": "Using row 4 of Pascal’s triangle, with coefficients $1,4,6,4,1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac1{\\sqrt2}+\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\right)^4&=\\frac14+\\frac2{\\sqrt6}+1+\\frac4{3\\sqrt6}+\\frac19\\\\\\left(\\frac1{\\sqrt2}+\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\right)^4&=\\frac{49}{36}+\\frac{10}{3\\sqrt6}\\\\\\left(\\frac1{\\sqrt2}+\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\right)^4&=\\frac{49}{36}+\\frac59\\sqrt6\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
